    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0742" n="484" xml:id="pg484"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1357</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        London</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-22T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1915, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department would like much to have exact, or at least approximate, number of
                    bales of American cotton seized by Great Britain first and last since the order
                    in council of March 11, and number of these for which to this time full payment
                    has been made.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
